{
  "title": "Split weird conventions tests into separate files",
  "description": "`puppeteer/tests/test_weird_conventions.py` has become a catch-all bundle of unrelated policy tests. That makes it hard to find a single convention, noisy to review, and awkward to keep growing. This PR moved the new private-Python-API ratchet into its own file as a first step; continue that cleanup for the existing conventions.\n\
\n\
Prefer one convention per file, or at least small domain-grouped files with a clear name, so reviewers can find and edit the relevant policy without opening an 800+ line bucket.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_weird_conventions.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_private_python_apis.py`\n\
- additional new `puppeteer/tests/test_*.py` files as conventions are split out",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
